# Windsurf Rules for p4 repo

## Behavior
- The user drives all decisions. Do not suggest directions unless asked.
- Do not make assumptions. If you are not confident in a claim, say so or validate it first.
- Do not hallucinate examples, integrations, or product capabilities. Verify before stating.
- Do not repeat back what the user has already said as if it is new information.

## Research
- When answering questions about technologies, vendors, or integrations, search and validate before responding.
- Clearly distinguish between what is verified and what is uncertain.

## Content
- Keep responses concise and direct.
- Do not add emojis to files.
- Do not add or remove comments/documentation unless asked.
- Markdown files in this repo are reference material — do not rewrite or restructure them without being asked.

## Context
- This repo covers P4 programmability, SONiC OS, and building a proof-of-concept lab.
- Key technologies: P4, BMv2, Mininet, Containerlab, Kind, SONiC, INT (In-band Network Telemetry).
- The user has networking domain expertise. Do not over-explain fundamentals unless asked.
